            <ArticleTitle>Impact of preterm birth on parental separation: a French population-based longitudinal study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e017845</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bmjopen-2017-017845</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The objective of this study was to investigate both the effects of low gestational age and infant's neurodevelopmental outcome at 2 years of age on the risk of parental separation within 7 years of giving birth.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Prospective.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">24 maternity clinics in the Pays-de-la-Loire region.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PARTICIPANTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">This study included 5732 infants delivered at &lt;35 weeks of gestation born between 2005 and 2013 who were enrolled in the population-based Loire Infant Follow-up Team cohort and who had a neurodevelopmental evaluation at 2 years. This neurodevelopmental evaluation was based on a physical examination, a psychomotor evaluation and a parent-completed questionnaire.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOME MEASURE" NlmCategory="METHODS">Risk of parental separation (parents living together or parents living separately).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Ten percent (572/5732) of the parents reported having undergone separation during the follow-up period. A mediation analysis showed that low gestational age had no direct effect on the risk of parental separation. Moreover, a non-optimal neurodevelopment at 2 years was associated with an increased risk of parental separation corresponding to a HR=1.49(1.23 to 1.80). Finally, the increased risk of parental separation was aggravated by low socioeconomic conditions.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The effect of low gestational age on the risk of parental separation was mediated by the infant's neurodevelopment.</AbstractText>
